  "paraphrase": "Princess Märtha Louise of Norway, the 52-year-old daughter of King Harald and Queen Sonja, married California-based practitioner Durek Verrett, 49, on Saturday in Geiranger. The ceremony, held at Hotel Union beneath the Geiranger fjord, combined traditional Norwegian church elements with a guest list of 350 that included European royalty and celebrities. Märtha Louise, who is fourth in line to the Norwegian throne, was attended by seven bridesmaids, including her two teenage daughters from her previous marriage to Norwegian author Ari Behn. The wedding drew spectators to the streets of the small village, despite overcast weather. The princess has pursued an unconventional royal path, previously identifying as clairvoyant and operating a healing school focused on angel communication. In 2022, she announced her withdrawal from official royal duties to concentrate on her business ventures with Verrett and to create separation between their work and the Norwegian royal institution. Verrett, who identifies as an energy activator and servant of God on social media, counts celebrities like Gwyneth Paltrow among his clientele, whom he has referred to as a 'soul sister'."
